<p>The superyacht Nord, linked to Russian billionaire Alexey Mordashov, crossed the blockaded Strait of Hormuz over the weekend after leaving Dubai, according to maritime-tracking data and a source close to Mordashov who spoke to Reuters. The waterway has faced severe restrictions during the U.S.-Iran conflict. The source said neither Iran nor the United States objected to the passage, while tracking reports placed Nord off Oman or in Muscat by Sunday.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/IJbyDr5AHve7eL8OamUM_wKtXRERoNFMILevxhOmFwjGWgHKfY39L-RwFGG5qykwnFW3C_zNbIoQ43B5TBE9HAsrWZ5NNC1ZA6JTOaI_YtiX04usExba2JEqyg45AUehwpVgG6J4dzFmD9_zzjTXpIOFAvVX173izIiApXo1otlFyhcN0fxWOftLzF-c6xjvYpjuaKTh' alt='The Nord anchored off Hong Kong in 2022.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Ownership records: Mordashov is not listed as the formal owner, but vessel records cited by Business Insider show a firm registered under his wife’s name held the yacht in 2022.</li><li>Cruise passages: Semafor reported that six cruise liners stranded in Gulf ports when the conflict began had also passed through the strait safely in recent weeks.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Representative for Alexey Mordashov: A representative for Mordashov declined to comment on how Nord received permission to use the restricted route, according to Thai PBS. (<a href='https://www.thaipbs.or.th/news/content/505225'>Thai PBS</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/28/alexei-mordashov-russian-superyacht-strait-of-hormuz'>Russian oligarch’s superyacht allowed through strait of Hormuz, source says</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/iran-and-us-allowed-russian-superyacht-cross-strait-hormuz-source-says'>Iran and US allowed Russian superyacht to cross Strait of Hormuz, source says</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cm2pn8zdxdjo'>Russian superyacht sails through Strait of Hormuz